    "style-research-extended vol.4 reggaeton — Assignment notes: \"Dominican dembow is a separate genre and is not claimed here — faster (115–130), a different snare cell, and a different roster (El Alfa, Tokischa, Chimbala, Rochy RD). If the app wants it, it needs its own genre model.\"",
    "style-research-extended vol.4 reggaeton — boundary rule: an act belongs to reggaeton if its rhythmic default is the dembow at 88–105 BPM; Dominican dembow is \"a different genre — faster, 115–130, with a different snare cell\"",
    "style-research-extended vol.4 dancehall — the dembow ancestor at 16th-grid precision: the Fish Market / \"Dem Bow\" cell at 16th indices 4, 7, 12, 15",
    "style-research-extended vol.4 — the archetypes this volume had to work around: `dominican-dembow` (El Alfa, Tokischa, Chimbala)",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dembow"
