  "notes": "⛔⛔ **`confidence` is `low`, and the protocol says a low model must state why: this one has a sourced BOUNDARY and an unsourced INTERIOR.** Volume 4's reggaeton section refuses it by name three times — *\"Dominican dembow is a separate genre and is not claimed here — faster (115–130), a different snare cell, and a different roster (El Alfa, Tokischa, Chimbala, Rochy RD). If the app wants it, it needs its own genre model\"* — and that sentence is the entire research this model has. The tempo band is sourced. The roster is sourced. *\"A different snare cell\"* is sourced as a **difference** and never as a cell. Everything below that line is inference and is marked here rather than left to be discovered. ▶ **What is authored, and on what basis.** The ancestor is shared and *is* documented: volume 4's dancehall grammar gives the Fish Market / \"Dem Bow\" figure at 16th-grid precision as indices **4, 7, 12, 15** — the 2, the a of 2, the 4 and the a of 4 — and `reggaeton` renders its own reading of it as `backbeat_24` with ghosts on `1a 2& 3a 4&`. This model takes the same backbeat and answers it on the **straight eighths** instead, at a high probability, with the machine-tight `quantizeStrength` of 0.94 and no swing. That is the shape the Dominican lane is known by — relentless, straighter and faster than the Puerto Rican one — and it is **inference from the sourced difference**, not a measurement. ⚠ **The invariant test therefore pins the two sourced claims and says which is which**: it runs faster than `reggaeton`, and its answer is not `reggaeton`'s. A future session with real Dominican-dembow research should expect to rewrite the interior of this model, and should not read the gate as evidence that the interior is right. ⚠ **Kick.** The ancestor's kick is *\"1 and 11, with the '&'-of-3 kick\"* — 1 and the a of 3 — and that is carried as `anchors: [\"1\"]` with a `secondaryAnchor` of `3` and a high `tresilloBias`, the same three knobs `reggaeton` uses, because the ancestor is shared even where the answer is not. ⚠ **Harmony is a bed and nothing more.** Two-chord minor vamps, few extensions, `vamp` weighted over everything — the lane's information is in the drums and the vocal, and authoring rich harmony here would be inventing a lane the records do not have. ⚠ **The harmony floor caught the first cut at 487 of the 500 distinct progressions a model must reach in 1,000 seeds, and the cure was authored difference rather than a looser gate.** Two changes, both inside the lane's own vocabulary: a third family (`i–VII–VI`, the one three-chord shape a dembow record plausibly plays) and `chordDurationBeats` widened to [2, 12]. That is nola-bounce's lesson applied — on a lane that sits on a vamp, **what varies is how long the loop sits, not what it sits on** — and it leaves the \"harmony is a bed\" rule intact. ⚠ **No vocal, so the chant this genre is built on is absent by construction.** The melodic parts are sparse and stab-shaped: a synth or brass hit answering the cell, `emptyBarBias` high, because a busy instrumental melody over this beat is a different genre.",
